becalmed:
Hush! the wind flags and fails--
Hush! they will lie becalmed in sight of strand--
Sight of my strand, where I do dwell alone;

becomin:
I like to see a man dress nice,
In clothes becomin' too;
I like to see a woman fix

beckons:
But positive, as sound.
It beckons and it baffles;
Philosophies don't know,

Perfect in bliss she from her heav'nly home
Looks down, and smiling beckons you to come;
Why then, fond parents, why these fruitless groans?
